 PCM integration – status

  We've connected ServiceNow to the PCM cashflow retrieval API (/api/ssgai/cashflows) using the svcnewsd service
  account, and built a reusable integration component so all our application scopes share one client.

  Working

  - Connection established and retrieving live data. The endpoint is only reachable via the MID server — the instance
    itself can't resolve the intranet host — and responses come back in ~700ms, so performance is not a concern.
  - The search criteria filter correctly server-side: an exact amount on an exact date returns exactly the one expected
    cashflow.
  - We've confirmed the request contract by testing: all seven criteria are mandatory, and Amount must be positive (PCM
    treats it as a magnitude, with Direction carrying the side). Our client handles that conversion.

  Blocker

  CounterpartyName is mandatory, but in dev every value is masked (e.g. CP Name (8577922)). A settlement email gives us
  the real counterparty name, never that token — so we can't currently drive a query from an actual email. Counterparty
  Reference looked like the fallback, but it's blank on 4 of the 6 rows returned.

  Everything else works; this single field blocks end-to-end matching.

  Questions

  1. Is the data unmasked in UAT/prod? (most important — if yes, this is a dev-only limitation)
  2. Is there a lookup from a real counterparty name to that masked ID?
  3. Could CounterpartyName be made optional or accept a wildcard? The other six criteria already narrow to a single
     row.
  4. Is there a bulk/batch variant? Currently it's one call per cashflow — ~290 cashflows means ~290 round trips.
  5. What does CaseNumber represent?
  6. Any update on the write-back API timeline?
